parameters.text:
=Analyze and triage the following insurance claim:

Claim ID: {{ $json.body.claim_id }}
Claimant ID: {{ $json.body.claimant_id }}
Category: {{ $json.body.category }}
Incident Description: {{ $json.body.incident_description }}
Claimed Amount: {{ $json.body.claimed_amount }}
Clause Code: {{ $json.body.clause_code }}
Item Age (Years): {{ $json.body.item_age_years }}
Has Police Report: {{ $json.body.has_police_report }}

Instructions:
1. Query coverage rules using the SearchPolicyTool for category '{{ $json.body.category }}' or clause '{{ $json.body.clause_code }}'.
2. Call FraudCheckTool with claimant ID '{{ $json.body.claimant_id }}', incident description, and claimed amount.
3. Call CalculatePayoutTool with claimed amount, clause code, item age, and police report flag. NEVER compute payout in your head.
4. Apply ClaimSentry Triaging Rules:
   - Set requires_human_review = true IF:
     a) calculated eligible_amount > 500.00 EUR, OR
     b) fraud risk_score >= 0.30, OR
     c) policy requires a police report and none was provided (has_police_report == false).
   - If requires_human_review is false and eligible_amount > 0, set recommendation = 'APPROVE'.
   - If eligible_amount == 0 and no coverage or rejected, set recommendation = 'REJECT'.
   - If escalated, set recommendation = 'ESCALATE'.
5. Produce the structured output JSON with complete justification.

parameters.jsonSchema:
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "claim_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The ID of the claim"
    },
    "recommendation": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": ["APPROVE", "REJECT", "ESCALATE"],
      "description": "Recommendation decision"
    },
    "requires_human_review": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "True if payout > 500 EUR, fraud risk >= 0.30, or missing mandatory police report"
    },
    "calculated_payout": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "Deterministic eligible payout amount from calculation tool"
    },
    "policy_code": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Applied policy clause code"
    },
    "fraud_risk_score": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "Evaluated fraud risk score from fraud tool"
    },
    "justification": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Detailed explanation citing policy clauses, calculations, and risk flags"
    }
  },
  "required": ["claim_id", "recommendation", "requires_human_review", "calculated_payout", "policy_code", "justification"]
}

